Source: libfprint-2-tod1-broadcom-installer
Section: admin
Maintainer: Daniel Iwugo <daniel@themalwarefiles.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.3
Homepage: https://github.com/elementmerc/latitude-fingerprint

Package: libfprint-2-tod1-broadcom-installer
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 libfprint-2-tod1 (>= 1:1.90.5+tod1),
 fprintd,
 libpam-fprintd,
 python3,
 python3-gi,
 libusb-1.0-0,
 ca-certificates,
 udev,
 curl | wget
Description: fetch and install the Broadcom CV3 fingerprint driver
 Dell Latitude and Precision laptops with the Broadcom BCM58200 ControlVault 3
 fingerprint sensor (USB 0a5c:5843) need a closed-source libfprint TOD driver
 that Canonical ships only for Ubuntu 22.04. This package makes that driver
 installable on newer Ubuntu releases.
 .
 The proprietary driver is not included here and is never redistributed by this
 package. On install it is downloaded from Canonical's archive, checked against
 a pinned SHA256 hash, and laid into the system. If the download fails the
 install fails loudly and changes nothing. See the homepage for the licensing
 rationale.
